    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2CYyGtgLvq5iRgHjYX2SJe6)_\n\n## Summary\n\n- Indicators L, F and N (links, files, notes) are bold, each in its own face (`sp-citar-indicator-link/file/note`).\n- Their colours come from the Modus palette (`blue`, `red`, `green`) via `modus-themes-get-color-value`, refreshed from `enable-theme-functions`, so they follow theme changes. Without Modus they inherit `font-lock-function-name-face`, `error` and `success`.\n- Citekey moved after the title and authors (into `suffix`), in the new `sp-citar-key` face (`shadow` + italic).\n- Padding: three spaces between template columns, two after each indicator.\n- `citar-indicators` is now set directly: the old `citar-symbols` setting is obsolete since citar 1.4 and was never read, which is why plain letters showed.\n- Docs updated in `docs/tangles/academic/sp-academic.org` (bullet lists); `sp-citations.el` is the matching tangle. No CHANGELOG edit.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Not run: no Emacs in the cloud container. Please try `citar-create-note` / `citar-open` and switch themes.\n- Branch name has no PR number prefix (cannot rename from the cloud session).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9m8fmtgNiBeMPZDGW)_",
